    "result_text": "All 274 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city title-casing rule for owner creation.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `NormalizeOwnerCity.java` (in `rest/function/owner/`):\n- Title-cases the owner's city (each whitespace-separated word: leading capital, rest lower-cased \u2014 so `\"new york\"` \u2192 `\"New York\"`).\n- But first scans existing owners; if any owner's city matches case-insensitively, it reuses that existing owner's exact spelling instead \u2014 keeping a city spelled consistently across all its owners.\n- Handles null/blank cities safely (leaves them untouched).\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`: inserted a `normalizeCity` step (under the `transaction` governance) after `ensureUnique` and before `assignCustomerCode`, so the customer-code step (which counts owners per city) sees the normalized, consistent city value.\n\nThe two new `Cp12Tests` pass: lowercase input `\"riverdale{n}\"` is returned as `\"Riverdale{n}\"`, and a second owner submitting the same city in a different case gets back the first owner's stored spelling. No existing tests regressed.",
